## Code Example
```javascript
// simple latency percentile calculator (pseudo)
function percentile(arr, p){
  arr.sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.ceil((arr.length-1)*p);
  return arr[idx];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this plan to handle schema evolution in the CSVs?
- What changes would you make to reduce tail latency if 95th percentile drifts upward during bursts?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of serverless vs. containerized performance under real-world burst scenarios, including cold-start effects, multi-region observability, and cost trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Cold-start impact on tail latency
- End-to-end latency measurement (P99)
- Autoscaling behavior across regions
- Cost implications of burst traffic
- Data strategy for realistic workloads

## Code Example

```javascript
async function measureLatency(url, trials = 100) {
  const start = Date.now();
  for (let i = 0; i < trials; i++) {
    await fetch(url, { cache: 'no-store' });
  }
  const end = Date.now();
  return (end - start) / trials;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you isolate cold-start latency from other backend delays in your telemetry?
- What specific metrics and dashboards would you use to validate cross-region SLA compliance during bursts?

